[E0431] Error: `arguments` is `Vec<Option<Argument>>`, which cannot be compared
    ╭─[ err/375_the_type_that_lacks_eq/main.wip:17:2 ]
    │
 15 │ @derive(Eq)
    │         ─┬
    │          ╰── `@derive(Eq)` writes the comparison field by field
    │
 17 │     arguments: Vec<Option<Argument>>
    │     ────────────────┬───────────────
    │                     ╰───────────────── not a comparable field
    │
    │ Help 1: `Vec<Option<Argument>>` implements `Eq` where `Option<Argument>` does, `Option<Argument>` where `Argument` does, and `Argument` does not
    │
    │ Help 2: write `@derive(Eq)` on `Argument` too, or an `extend` block that implements `Eq` for it
    │
    │ Note: a field is comparable when it is a number, a `bool`, a `str`, a `cstring`, a `ptr<T>`, an array of those, or a type that implements `Eq`
────╯
